        "date": "2026-09-24T03:20:09Z"
      },
      "message": "Rename to OrcaSAQ2: package, entry point, image and paths\n\nThe plugin shipped under its internal working name (orca_exl3 / Orca-Qtip-SAQ-Kernel),\nwhich nothing user-facing calls it. Everything exposed is now OrcaSAQ2:\n\n  pip name      orca-exl3        -> orcasaq2-kernel\n  module        orca_exl3        -> orcasaq2\n  entry point   orca_exl3        -> orcasaq2\n  image         orca-exl3-vllm   -> orcasaq2-vllm\n  in-container  /opt/orca-exl3   -> /opt/orcasaq2\n\nAlso makes the package actually installable for the native path. patches/ sat outside\nthe package while setuptools was told `packages = [\"orca_exl3\"]`, so `pip install` gave\nusers the vLLM plugin and silently no embedding patch -- the exllamav3 route was\nundocumentedly broken for anyone who did not clone the repo. It now lives at\norcasaq2/patches and installs with the rest.\n\nexllamav3 is checked at plugin registration instead of at the first GEMM. It is not on\nPyPI and cannot be a declared dependency (the wheel is ABI-linked to both torch and the\nCUDA major version), so the check raises with the two commands needed to pick the right\nrelease asset, rather than letting a bare ModuleNotFoundError surface from inside a\ncustom op on the first request.\n\nVerified: package imports, the patch applies to the installed exllamav3, all three\npresets source and assemble correct arguments, shell syntax clean.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
