    "sha": "a514f85b09afe827ffc55a8e18e0808cd8fdbd24",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOUocPUNoAKGE1MTRmODViMDlhZmU4MjdmZmM1NWE4ZTE4ZTA4MDhjZDhmZGJkMjQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "kai.shen",
        "email": "kai.shen@myflashcloud.com",
        "date": "2026-09-23T16:29:51Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "kai.shen",
        "email": "kai.shen@myflashcloud.com",
        "date": "2026-09-23T16:29:51Z"
      },
      "message": "Fix silent zeroing of the int8 embedding scales under deferred load\n\nThe native path shipped broken: every token embedded to zero, so exllamav3 emitted a\nstream of \"!\" and nothing else. It loaded, it ran, it was fast, and it was garbage.\n\nInside model.load() exllamav3 runs a DEFERRED load -- get_tensor returns an unfilled\nzeroed tensor immediately, queues the read, and fills that same tensor object later.\nThe patch stored qweight by reference, so the fill reached it; scales went through\n.to(out_dtype), which copied the still-zero buffer, and the fill landed in a tensor\nnobody held. qweight was right, scales were 0, every row came out 0.\n\nBoth tensors now load with no_defer=True, and the dtype cast moved to forward() where\nit acts on the gathered rows. Reading eagerly costs a one-off load pause and makes the\ntensors safe to touch, which the alias approach never was -- any later .to(), .clone()\nor non-view reshape would silently reintroduce this.\n\nVerified after the fix: scales 248320/248320 non-zero; embedding rel err vs the bf16\nbase 0.0247 (the int8 quantization error, as intended); \"The capital of France is\" ->\n\" Paris.\\nThe capital of Germany is Berlin. ...\" instead of \"!!!!!!\".\n\nCaught by benchmarking, not by the unit check -- the unit check built the table from\ntensors it had loaded itself, outside a deferred-load bracket, so it could never see\nthis.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>",
